Issue2PR database migrations (Alembic, async)
=============================================

This directory holds the Alembic migration environment. It is wired to the
async engine built from ``settings.database_url`` and targets the ORM models in
``app/db/models.py`` (``Base.metadata``).

Prerequisites
-------------
Install the server extras (includes SQLAlchemy, asyncpg, and Alembic)::

    pip install -e ".[server]"

A reachable PostgreSQL instance matching ``DATABASE_URL`` in your ``.env`` is
required for online migrations, e.g.::

    postgresql+asyncpg://issue2pr:issue2pr@localhost:5432/issue2pr

Common commands
---------------
Autogenerate a new revision by diffing the DB against the models::

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"

Apply migrations up to the latest revision::

    alembic upgrade head

Roll back one revision::

    alembic downgrade -1

Notes
-----
* The database URL is injected at runtime from ``Settings`` in ``env.py``; you
  do not need to (and should not) hardcode credentials in ``alembic.ini``.
* ``compare_type=True`` is enabled so column type changes are detected during
  autogenerate.
* Generated revision scripts are written to the ``versions/`` subdirectory.
* For local development without Postgres, ``app.db.session.create_all()`` can
  create the schema directly from the models (not a substitute for migrations
  in production).
